Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:37:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 05/19] HIP GCN: q6_K matvec for 1-3 columns

mmvq-gcn.cu: one wave per 2 rows, each lane decoding the same 16 weights of every 4th block from fixed
offsets, activations loaded once for both rows (the generic kernel spends ~67 instructions per 8 q6_K
weights on gfx900). Row-pair kernels at 1 and 3 columns: two rows per 32-bit multiply, loads first behind
a scheduling barrier, activations shared through LDS (found with rocprofv3 counters). Gate + GLU fused.

MI25, q6_K 12288x4096: 197 -> 250 GB/s at 1 column; 3 columns 156.5 -> 143.1 us with the LDS row-pair.
Qwen3.5 9B writing 33.4 -> 36.7 t/s at 21k. GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_GCN=0 turns it off, GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_GCN_PAIR=0
the row-pair kernels.

